    "final_answer": "I have all the information needed. Let me compile the answer.\n\n## Answer\n\nI found a course on Coursera that provides an introduction to Psychology. Here are the details:\n\n**Course Title:** Introduction to Psychology (心理学入门)\n\n- **Instructor:** Paul Bloom\n- **Institution:** Yale University\n- **Approximate Time to Complete:** Approximately **20 hours total** (the course is designed to be completed in 2 weeks at 10 hours per week of study)\n\n**Additional details about the course:**\n- It consists of **7 modules**\n- Level: **Beginner** (no prior experience required)\n- Rated **4.9 out of 5 stars** (based on 32,692 reviews)\n- Over **1,637,104 students** enrolled\n- Includes **6 assignments**\n- Taught in English (with subtitles available in 25 languages, including Simplified Chinese)\n- Flexible schedule — learn at your own pace\n- Offers a shareable certificate upon completion\n\nThis is a popular, highly-rated introductory psychology course offered by Yale University, taught by Professor Paul Bloom, well-known for his work in psychology and cognitive science.",
